{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id24892375"}, "name":{"label":"SenseiPhil"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2024-05-14T06:18:55-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"5.4.2"}, "id":{"label":"11266404117"}, "title":{"label":"Offline maps and hiking done right"}, "content":{"label":"I have two apps that track my walks. Withings because of my watch, and Pedometer++. Why use both? I need the heart rate from Withings but everything else to do with steps, pace, mapping I need Pedometer++. \n\nThere is only one feature from tracking walks that I need. I sometimes forget to stop tracking. I then drive home and have all that distance added. If I could trim the end by timestamp it would fix it. Withings and Strava let me - just would be icing on the cake if Pedometer++ did. \n\nThanks David.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=712286167&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"2"}}, 
